    {
      "id": "s_ec4_14y",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 76,
      "y": 40009,
      "props": {
        "w": 630,
        "h": 19,
        "html": "Lateral-torsional buckling (EN 1994-1-1 §6.4.1(1); EN 1993-1-1 §6.3.2.2)",
        "fontFamily": "Roboto",
        "fontSize": 13,
        "color": "#475569",
        "align": "left"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s_ec4_14z",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 76,
      "y": 40034,
      "props": {
        "w": 630,
        "h": 19,
        "html": "EN 1994-1-1 §6.4.1(1): a steel flange attached to the slab by shear connection to §6.6 may be",
        "fontFamily": "Roboto",
        "fontSize": 13,
        "color": "#475569",
        "align": "left"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s_ec4_150",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 76,
      "y": 40059,
      "props": {
        "w": 630,
        "h": 19,
        "html": "taken as laterally stable if the slab is laterally stable. Applied when s ≤ s_max (§6.6.5.5);",
        "fontFamily": "Roboto",
        "fontSize": 13,
        "color": "#475569",
        "align": "left"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s_ec4_151",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 76,
      "y": 40084,
      "props": {
        "w": 630,
        "h": 19,
        "html": "L_LT is then the stud spacing (χ_LT = 1). Otherwise the full span is used as unrestrained.",
        "fontFamily": "Roboto",
        "fontSize": 13,
        "color": "#475569",
        "align": "left"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "s_ec4_152",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 76,
